4	ICMP	192.168.1.10	8.8.8.8	Echo request
5	ICMP	8.8.8.8	192.168.1.10	Echo reply

Packet Details Observed
When a packet is selected, Wireshark may show:
1. Frame: Captured frame length and interface information.
2. Ethernet II: Source and destination MAC addresses.
3. Internet Protocol (IP): Source and destination IP addresses.
4. TCP/UDP: Source and destination port numbers.
5. Application protocol: Application-specific data, such as DNS queries or responses.

Result
Wireshark was studied as a packet capture and network analysis tool. Network packets were captured and analyzed using display filters, and encapsulation at the application, transport, network, data link, and physical layers of the protocol stack was understood.
